{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>But he would not, etc.</b> The verse's saying <b>But he would not</b> — meaning: although there was reason for Him to listen, given the branches of sin in which Balaam was entangled, nevertheless HaShem was appeased without reason and did not listen, etc., and He gave the reason: ״כִּי אֲהֵבְךָ ה׳״ — meaning, not on account of your being worthy of this thing. And see what I explained in the verse ״וְלֹא אָבָה סִיחוֹן״ (Deuteronomy 2:30)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:39.956521273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}